<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">3 </span>Critical pairs in <math id="S3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{V}\times R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖵</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{V}\times R</annotation></semantics></math></h2>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The following lemma gives the two cases used below.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3.1</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> be a poset and let <math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x,y\in R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x,y\in R</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
<ol id="S3.I1" class="ltx_enumerate ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="S3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(i)</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For each </span><math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in\{p,q\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in\{p,q\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, the pair
</span><math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl((0,x),(s,y)\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl((0,x),(s,y)\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is critical in </span><math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{V}\times R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖵</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{V}\times R</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> if and
only if</span></p>
<table id="S3.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x\nleq_{R}y,\quad\mathord{\downarrow}^{\!\circ}x\subseteq\downarrow y,\quad\mathord{\uparrow}^{\!\circ}y\subseteq\uparrow x." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≰</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>R</mi></msub><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">↓</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msup><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0em">⊆</mo><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">↓</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">↑</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msup><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0em">⊆</mo><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">↑</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\nleq_{R}y,\quad\mathord{\downarrow}^{\!\circ}x\subseteq\downarrow y,\quad\mathord{\uparrow}^{\!\circ}y\subseteq\uparrow x.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(ii)</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For distinct </span><math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s,t\in\{p,q\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s,t\in\{p,q\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, the pair
</span><math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl((s,x),(t,y)\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl((s,x),(t,y)\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is critical in </span><math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{V}\times R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖵</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{V}\times R</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> if and
only if</span></p>
<table id="S3.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x\leq_{R}y,\quad x\in\Min(R),\quad y\in\Max(R)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>R</mi></msub><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>Min</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>Max</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\leq_{R}y,\quad x\in\Min(R),\quad y\in\Max(R).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">For (i), the two product points are
incomparable if and only if <math id="S3.p2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x\nleq_{R}y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≰</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>R</mi></msub><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\nleq_{R}y</annotation></semantics></math>. The conditions in
(<a href="#S2.E3" title="In 2 Preliminaries ‣ The Kelly–Trotter product conjecture for posets of dimension three" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>) give the two remaining inclusions in
(<a href="#S3.E5" title="In item (i) ‣ Lemma 3.1. ‣ 3 Critical pairs in 𝖵×𝑅 ‣ The Kelly–Trotter product conjecture for posets of dimension three" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>).
For (ii), incomparability is automatic because
<math id="S3.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p\parallel_{\mathsf{V}}q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\parallel_{\mathsf{V}}q</annotation></semantics></math>. The remaining conditions in
(<a href="#S2.E3" title="In 2 Preliminaries ‣ The Kelly–Trotter product conjecture for posets of dimension three" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>) are exactly
(<a href="#S3.E6" title="In item (ii) ‣ Lemma 3.1. ‣ 3 Critical pairs in 𝖵×𝑅 ‣ The Kelly–Trotter product conjecture for posets of dimension three" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="S3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\Min(R)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\Min(R)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in\Max(R)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in\Max(R)</annotation></semantics></math>, then
(<a href="#S3.E5" title="In item (i) ‣ Lemma 3.1. ‣ 3 Critical pairs in 𝖵×𝑅 ‣ The Kelly–Trotter product conjecture for posets of dimension three" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>) reduces to <math id="S3.p3.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x\nleq_{R}y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≰</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>R</mi></msub><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\nleq_{R}y</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let</p>
<table id="S3.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=\bigl((s,x),(t,y)\bigr),\qquad\beta=\bigl((s^{\prime},x^{\prime}),(t^{\prime},y^{\prime})\bigr)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=\bigl((s,x),(t,y)\bigr),\qquad\beta=\bigl((s^{\prime},x^{\prime}),(t^{\prime},y^{\prime})\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">be distinct critical pairs in <math id="S3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{V}\times R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖵</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{V}\times R</annotation></semantics></math>. Since the product
order is coordinatewise, by (<a href="#S2.E4" title="In 2 Preliminaries ‣ The Kelly–Trotter product conjecture for posets of dimension three" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>), we have</p>
<table id="S3.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\alpha\sim\beta\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad s\leq_{\mathsf{V}}t^{\prime},\quad s^{\prime}\leq_{\mathsf{V}}t,\quad x\leq_{R}y^{\prime},\quad x^{\prime}\leq_{R}y." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟺</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mi>t</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>s</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>R</mi></msub><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>x</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>R</mi></msub><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\sim\beta\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad s\leq_{\mathsf{V}}t^{\prime},\quad s^{\prime}\leq_{\mathsf{V}}t,\quad x\leq_{R}y^{\prime},\quad x^{\prime}\leq_{R}y.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p3.3" class="ltx_p">In the applications below, the first two comparisons in
(<a href="#S3.E7" title="In 3 Critical pairs in 𝖵×𝑅 ‣ The Kelly–Trotter product conjecture for posets of dimension three" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>) follow immediately from <math id="S3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;p</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;q</annotation></semantics></math>, or
equality. Thus only the last two comparisons need to be checked
explicitly.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 3.2</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> be a poset with <math id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dim R=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">dim</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dim R=3</annotation></semantics></math>. If at least one of
<math id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma(\mathsf{V}\times R)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖵</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma(\mathsf{V}\times R)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma(\mathsf{V}^{d}\times R)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝖵</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma(\mathsf{V}^{d}\times R)</annotation></semantics></math> is not
<math id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>-colorable, then
<math id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dim(C_{k}\times R)=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">dim</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dim(C_{k}\times R)=4</annotation></semantics></math> for every <math id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Corollary <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem2" title="Corollary 2.2. ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ The Kelly–Trotter product conjecture for posets of dimension three" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a>, we have <math id="S3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dim(\mathsf{V}\times R)\geq 4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">dim</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖵</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dim(\mathsf{V}\times R)\geq 4</annotation></semantics></math> or
<math id="S3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dim(\mathsf{V}^{d}\times R)\geq 4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">dim</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝖵</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dim(\mathsf{V}^{d}\times R)\geq 4</annotation></semantics></math>. Since every <math id="S3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> contains copies of
both <math id="S3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖵</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{V}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{V}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝖵</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{V}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, monotonicity gives
<math id="S3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dim(C_{k}\times R)\geq 4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">dim</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dim(C_{k}\times R)\geq 4</annotation></semantics></math>. The reverse inequality follows from
(<a href="#S1.E2" title="In 1 Introduction ‣ The Kelly–Trotter product conjecture for posets of dimension three" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) with <math id="S3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X=R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=R</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>The six infinite families</h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The classification contains six infinite families
<math id="S4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{n},F_{n},G_{n},H_{n},I_{n},J_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{n},F_{n},G_{n},H_{n},I_{n},J_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. For each member <math id="S4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> of these families,
the corresponding subsection gives a labeled Hasse diagram of <math id="S4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>
and two tables defining a graph <math id="S4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>. The left table lists the
vertices of <math id="S4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> as ordered pairs in <math id="S4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{V}\times R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖵</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{V}\times R</annotation></semantics></math>. In the
right table, every vertex in the first column is adjacent to every
vertex in the second column, with the stated range applying to the
entire row. Each adjacency is recorded only once. We write
<math id="S4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\sim y_{1},\ldots,y_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\sim y_{1},\ldots,y_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> to mean that <math id="S4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> is adjacent to each of
<math id="S4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{1},\ldots,y_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{1},\ldots,y_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 4.1</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For every <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and every <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\in\{E_{n},F_{n},G_{n},H_{n},I_{n},J_{n}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\in\{E_{n},F_{n},G_{n},H_{n},I_{n},J_{n}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, the graph <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma(\mathsf{V}\times R)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖵</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma(\mathsf{V}\times R)</annotation></semantics></math> is not <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>-colorable.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.1 </span>The family <math id="S4.SS1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{n}</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

