<div id="S4.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 4.2</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For every <math id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{E_{n}}\subseteq\Gamma(\mathsf{V}\times E_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖵</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{E_{n}}\subseteq\Gamma(\mathsf{V}\times E_{n})</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{E_{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{E_{n}}</annotation></semantics></math> is not
<math id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>-colorable.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="S4.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Critical pairs.</em>
The minimal and maximal elements of <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> are</p>
<table id="S4.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Min(E_{n})=\{a_{i}:1\leq i\leq n+2\}\cup\{c\},\qquad\Max(E_{n})=\{b_{1},b_{n+3},d\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Min(E_{n})=\{a_{i}:1\leq i\leq n+2\}\cup\{c\},\qquad\Max(E_{n})=\{b_{1},b_{n+3},d\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">For <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, condition (<a href="#S3.E5" title="In item (i) ‣ Lemma 3.1. ‣ 3 Critical pairs in 𝖵×𝑅 ‣ The Kelly–Trotter product conjecture for posets of dimension three" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>) follows
from</p>
<table id="S4.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}\nleq c,\qquad\mathord{\downarrow}^{\!\circ}a_{i}=\varnothing,\qquad\mathord{\uparrow}^{\!\circ}c=\{d\}\subseteq\uparrow a_{i}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≰</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">↓</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">↑</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}\nleq c,\qquad\mathord{\downarrow}^{\!\circ}a_{i}=\varnothing,\qquad\mathord{\uparrow}^{\!\circ}c=\{d\}\subseteq\uparrow a_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p3.3" class="ltx_p">For <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\nleq b_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>≰</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\nleq b_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S4.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathord{\downarrow}^{\!\circ}c=\varnothing" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">↓</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathord{\downarrow}^{\!\circ}c=\varnothing</annotation></semantics></math>. The element <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is maximal when
<math id="S4.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=n+3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=n+3</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\leq i\leq n+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\leq i\leq n+2</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="S4.SS1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathord{\uparrow}^{\!\circ}b_{i}=\{d\}\subseteq\uparrow c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">↑</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathord{\uparrow}^{\!\circ}b_{i}=\{d\}\subseteq\uparrow c</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus
(<a href="#S3.E5" title="In item (i) ‣ Lemma 3.1. ‣ 3 Critical pairs in 𝖵×𝑅 ‣ The Kelly–Trotter product conjecture for posets of dimension three" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>) also holds for every <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For each of <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{1},\ldots,\ell_{6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>6</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{1},\ldots,\ell_{6}</annotation></semantics></math>, the first <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>-coordinate
is minimal, the second is maximal, and the two are incomparable.
Hence (<a href="#S3.E5" title="In item (i) ‣ Lemma 3.1. ‣ 3 Critical pairs in 𝖵×𝑅 ‣ The Kelly–Trotter product conjecture for posets of dimension three" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>) holds for these six vertices.
For <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, condition (<a href="#S3.E5" title="In item (i) ‣ Lemma 3.1. ‣ 3 Critical pairs in 𝖵×𝑅 ‣ The Kelly–Trotter product conjecture for posets of dimension three" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>)
follows from</p>
<table id="S4.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{array}[]{llll}r_{1}:&amp;b_{1}\nleq d,&amp;\mathord{\downarrow}^{\!\circ}b_{1}=\{a_{1}\}\subseteq\downarrow d,&amp;\mathord{\uparrow}^{\!\circ}d=\varnothing,\\
r_{2}:&amp;b_{n+3}\nleq d,&amp;\mathord{\downarrow}^{\!\circ}b_{n+3}=\{a_{n+2}\}\subseteq\downarrow d,&amp;\mathord{\uparrow}^{\!\circ}d=\varnothing.\end{array}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≰</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">↓</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">↑</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≰</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">↓</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">↑</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{array}[]{llll}r_{1}:&amp;b_{1}\nleq d,&amp;\mathord{\downarrow}^{\!\circ}b_{1}=\{a_{1}\}\subseteq\downarrow d,&amp;\mathord{\uparrow}^{\!\circ}d=\varnothing,\\
r_{2}:&amp;b_{n+3}\nleq d,&amp;\mathord{\downarrow}^{\!\circ}b_{n+3}=\{a_{n+2}\}\subseteq\downarrow d,&amp;\mathord{\uparrow}^{\!\circ}d=\varnothing.\end{array}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p3.4" class="ltx_p">By Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 3.1. ‣ 3 Critical pairs in 𝖵×𝑅 ‣ The Kelly–Trotter product conjecture for posets of dimension three" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>(i),
<math id="S4.SS1.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{i},\gamma_{i},\ell_{1},\ldots,\ell_{6},r_{1},r_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{i},\gamma_{i},\ell_{1},\ldots,\ell_{6},r_{1},r_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> are critical pairs.
Since <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}\leq d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}\leq d</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\leq d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\leq d</annotation></semantics></math>,
Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 3.1. ‣ 3 Critical pairs in 𝖵×𝑅 ‣ The Kelly–Trotter product conjecture for posets of dimension three" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>(ii) shows that
<math id="S4.SS1.p3.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i},\pi_{1},\pi_{2},\pi_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i},\pi_{1},\pi_{2},\pi_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> are critical pairs.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="S4.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Edges.</em>
For every adjacency in the right table, the two <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>-comparisons
in (<a href="#S3.E7" title="In 3 Critical pairs in 𝖵×𝑅 ‣ The Kelly–Trotter product conjecture for posets of dimension three" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>) are</p>
<table id="S4.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}\leq b_{i},\qquad a_{i}\leq b_{i+1},\qquad c\leq d,\qquad a_{i}\leq d," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}\leq b_{i},\qquad a_{i}\leq b_{i+1},\qquad c\leq d,\qquad a_{i}\leq d,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">or equalities. These comparisons follow from the Hasse diagram of
<math id="S4.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence</p>
<table id="S4.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{E_{n}}\subseteq\Gamma(\mathsf{V}\times E_{n})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖵</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{E_{n}}\subseteq\Gamma(\mathsf{V}\times E_{n}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Suppose that <math id="S4.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math> is a proper <math id="S4.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>-coloring of <math id="S4.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{E_{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{E_{n}}</annotation></semantics></math>
with colors <math id="S4.SS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0,1,2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0,1,2</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Claim 1.</span>
<math id="S4.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(\pi_{1})=\varphi(\pi_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(\pi_{1})=\varphi(\pi_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Assume otherwise. We may take <math id="S4.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(\pi_{1})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(\pi_{1})=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(\pi_{2})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(\pi_{2})=1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Every <math id="S4.SS1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is adjacent to both <math id="S4.SS1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus <math id="S4.SS1.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(\beta_{i})=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(\beta_{i})=2</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S4.SS1.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq i\leq n+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq i\leq n+2</annotation></semantics></math>.
The vertex <math id="S4.SS1.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> is also adjacent to both, so
<math id="S4.SS1.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(\pi_{3})=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(\pi_{3})=2</annotation></semantics></math>. The right table gives
<math id="S4.SS1.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{1}\sim\beta_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{1}\sim\beta_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S4.SS1.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{i}\sim\beta_{i-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{i}\sim\beta_{i-1}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S4.SS1.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\leq i\leq n+3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\leq i\leq n+3</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence
<math id="S4.SS1.p7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(\gamma_{i})\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(\gamma_{i})\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S4.SS1.p7.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq i\leq n+3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq i\leq n+3</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="S4.SS1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq i\leq n+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq i\leq n+2</annotation></semantics></math>, the vertex <math id="S4.SS1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is adjacent to
<math id="S4.SS1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{i},\gamma_{i+1},\pi_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{i},\gamma_{i+1},\pi_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>. The vertices <math id="S4.SS1.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S4.SS1.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{i+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{i+1}</annotation></semantics></math> have the same color. Otherwise <math id="S4.SS1.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> would
have neighbors of all three colors. Thus</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(\gamma_{1})=\cdots=\varphi(\gamma_{n+3})=t" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(\gamma_{1})=\cdots=\varphi(\gamma_{n+3})=t</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">for some <math id="S4.SS1.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Suppose first that <math id="S4.SS1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex21X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
