<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex22X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Longrightarrow\varphi(\alpha_{n+2})=0," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Longrightarrow\varphi(\alpha_{n+2})=0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex22Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex22Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ell_{4}\sim\alpha_{n+2},\pi_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ell_{4}\sim\alpha_{n+2},\pi_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex22Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Longrightarrow\varphi(\ell_{4})=2," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Longrightarrow\varphi(\ell_{4})=2,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex22Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex22Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r_{2}\sim\ell_{4},\gamma_{n+3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r_{2}\sim\ell_{4},\gamma_{n+3}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex22Xb.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Longrightarrow\varphi(r_{2})=0," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Longrightarrow\varphi(r_{2})=0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex22Xc"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex22Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ell_{6}\sim r_{2},\beta_{n+2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ell_{6}\sim r_{2},\beta_{n+2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex22Xc.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Longrightarrow\varphi(\ell_{6})=1." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Longrightarrow\varphi(\ell_{6})=1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Both <math id="S4.SS1.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS1.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> are adjacent to <math id="S4.SS1.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{6}</annotation></semantics></math>, so neither
has color <math id="S4.SS1.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S4.SS1.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{1}\sim\gamma_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{1}\sim\gamma_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we also have
<math id="S4.SS1.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(r_{1})\neq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(r_{1})\neq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="S4.SS1.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(r_{1})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(r_{1})=0</annotation></semantics></math>, then
<math id="S4.SS1.p11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(\ell_{3})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(\ell_{3})=1</annotation></semantics></math>, since <math id="S4.SS1.p11.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{3}\sim r_{1},\beta_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{3}\sim r_{1},\beta_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. If
<math id="S4.SS1.p11.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(r_{1})=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(r_{1})=2</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S4.SS1.p11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(\ell_{2})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(\ell_{2})=1</annotation></semantics></math>, since
<math id="S4.SS1.p11.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2}\sim r_{1},\pi_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2}\sim r_{1},\pi_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Both conclusions are impossible. This proves
Claim 1.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Claim 1, we may take</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(\pi_{1})=\varphi(\pi_{2})=0,\qquad\varphi(\pi_{3})=1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(\pi_{1})=\varphi(\pi_{2})=0,\qquad\varphi(\pi_{3})=1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p13" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Claim 2.</span>
<math id="S4.SS1.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(\gamma_{i})\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(\gamma_{i})\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math> for every <math id="S4.SS1.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq i\leq n+3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq i\leq n+3</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">Suppose that <math id="S4.SS1.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(\gamma_{j})=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(\gamma_{j})=2</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="S4.SS1.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>. Fix
<math id="S4.SS1.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq i\leq n+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq i\leq n+2</annotation></semantics></math>.
If <math id="S4.SS1.p14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(\gamma_{i})=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(\gamma_{i})=2</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S4.SS1.p14.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(\beta_{i})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(\beta_{i})=1</annotation></semantics></math>, since <math id="S4.SS1.p14.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i}\sim\gamma_{i},\pi_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i}\sim\gamma_{i},\pi_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The edge
<math id="S4.SS1.p14.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i}\sim\gamma_{i+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i}\sim\gamma_{i+1}</annotation></semantics></math> excludes color <math id="S4.SS1.p14.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> from
<math id="S4.SS1.p14.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{i+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{i+1}</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="S4.SS1.p14.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(\gamma_{i+1})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(\gamma_{i+1})=0</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S4.SS1.p14.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>
would have neighbors of all three colors. Thus
<math id="S4.SS1.p14.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(\gamma_{i+1})=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(\gamma_{i+1})=2</annotation></semantics></math>. The reverse implication follows in the
same way. Therefore</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\varphi(\gamma_{i})=2\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad\varphi(\gamma_{i+1})=2." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟺</mo><mi>φ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(\gamma_{i})=2\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad\varphi(\gamma_{i+1})=2.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p14.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p14.2.1" class="ltx_text">The equivalence holds for every <math id="S4.SS1.p14.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, so</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(\gamma_{i})=2\qquad(1\leq i\leq n+3)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(\gamma_{i})=2\qquad(1\leq i\leq n+3).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p14.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p14.3.1" class="ltx_text">The adjacencies <math id="S4.SS1.p14.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i}\sim\pi_{1},\gamma_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i}\sim\pi_{1},\gamma_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> imply</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(\beta_{i})=1\qquad(1\leq i\leq n+2)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(\beta_{i})=1\qquad(1\leq i\leq n+2).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S4.SS1.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{1}\sim\gamma_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{1}\sim\gamma_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have
<math id="S4.SS1.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(r_{1})\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(r_{1})\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="S4.SS1.p15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(r_{1})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(r_{1})=0</annotation></semantics></math>, then
<math id="S4.SS1.p15.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(\ell_{3})=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(\ell_{3})=2</annotation></semantics></math>, since <math id="S4.SS1.p15.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{3}\sim r_{1},\beta_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{3}\sim r_{1},\beta_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. If
<math id="S4.SS1.p15.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(r_{1})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(r_{1})=1</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S4.SS1.p15.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(\ell_{2})=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(\ell_{2})=2</annotation></semantics></math>, since
<math id="S4.SS1.p15.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2}\sim r_{1},\pi_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2}\sim r_{1},\pi_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus at least one of <math id="S4.SS1.p15.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2},\ell_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2},\ell_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> has
color <math id="S4.SS1.p15.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text">The vertex <math id="S4.SS1.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{6}</annotation></semantics></math> is adjacent to <math id="S4.SS1.p16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{n+2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{n+2}</annotation></semantics></math>, which has color
<math id="S4.SS1.p16.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>, and to a vertex of color <math id="S4.SS1.p16.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> in
<math id="S4.SS1.p16.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\ell_{2},\ell_{3}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\ell_{2},\ell_{3}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus <math id="S4.SS1.p16.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(\ell_{6})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(\ell_{6})=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Each of
<math id="S4.SS1.p16.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2},\ell_{3},r_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2},\ell_{3},r_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is adjacent to <math id="S4.SS1.p16.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{6}</annotation></semantics></math>, so none has color
<math id="S4.SS1.p16.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>. Since
<math id="S4.SS1.p16.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{2}\sim\gamma_{n+3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{2}\sim\gamma_{n+3}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="S4.SS1.p16.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(r_{2})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(r_{2})=1</annotation></semantics></math>. The neighbors of
<math id="S4.SS1.p16.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{5}</annotation></semantics></math> include <math id="S4.SS1.p16.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> of color <math id="S4.SS1.p16.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS1.p16.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> of color <math id="S4.SS1.p16.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>,
and a vertex of color <math id="S4.SS1.p16.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S4.SS1.p16.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\ell_{2},\ell_{3}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\ell_{2},\ell_{3}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus <math id="S4.SS1.p16.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{5}</annotation></semantics></math>
has neighbors of all three colors, a contradiction. This proves Claim 2.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p17" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Claim 3.</span>
One of <math id="S4.SS1.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2},\ell_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2},\ell_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> has color <math id="S4.SS1.p17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p18" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p18.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p18.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S4.SS1.p18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{1}\sim\pi_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{1}\sim\pi_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have
<math id="S4.SS1.p18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(\ell_{1})\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(\ell_{1})\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Suppose <math id="S4.SS1.p18.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(r_{1})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(r_{1})=1</annotation></semantics></math>. By Claim 2 and
<math id="S4.SS1.p18.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{1}\sim\gamma_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{1}\sim\gamma_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="S4.SS1.p18.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(\gamma_{1})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(\gamma_{1})=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Since
<math id="S4.SS1.p18.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{1}\sim\pi_{1},r_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{1}\sim\pi_{1},r_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="S4.SS1.p18.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(\ell_{1})=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(\ell_{1})=2</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus
<math id="S4.SS1.p18.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> has neighbors <math id="S4.SS1.p18.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{1},\pi_{3},\ell_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{1},\pi_{3},\ell_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> of colors
<math id="S4.SS1.p18.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0,1,2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0,1,2</annotation></semantics></math>, a contradiction.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p19" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p19.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p19.1.1" class="ltx_text">Hence <math id="S4.SS1.p19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(r_{1})\in\{0,2\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(r_{1})\in\{0,2\}</annotation></semantics></math>. If
<math id="S4.SS1.p19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(r_{1})=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(r_{1})=2</annotation></semantics></math>, the neighbors <math id="S4.SS1.p19.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{1},r_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{1},r_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> of
<math id="S4.SS1.p19.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> have colors <math id="S4.SS1.p19.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0,2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0,2</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S4.SS1.p19.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(\ell_{2})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(\ell_{2})=1</annotation></semantics></math>. If
<math id="S4.SS1.p19.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(r_{1})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(r_{1})=0</annotation></semantics></math>, Claim 2 and <math id="S4.SS1.p19.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{1}\sim\gamma_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{1}\sim\gamma_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> imply
<math id="S4.SS1.p19.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(\gamma_{1})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(\gamma_{1})=1</annotation></semantics></math>. The adjacencies
<math id="S4.SS1.p19.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1}\sim\gamma_{1},\pi_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1}\sim\gamma_{1},\pi_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S4.SS1.p19.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{3}\sim r_{1},\beta_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{3}\sim r_{1},\beta_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> imply
<math id="S4.SS1.p19.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(\beta_{1})=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(\beta_{1})=2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS1.p19.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(\ell_{3})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(\ell_{3})=1</annotation></semantics></math>.
This proves Claim 3.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p20" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.p20.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p20.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Claim 4.</span>
<math id="S4.SS1.p20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(r_{2})\neq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(r_{2})\neq 1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p21" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p21.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p21.1.1" class="ltx_text">Assume otherwise. Claim 2 and
<math id="S4.SS1.p21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{2}\sim\gamma_{n+3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{2}\sim\gamma_{n+3}</annotation></semantics></math> imply <math id="S4.SS1.p21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(\gamma_{n+3})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(\gamma_{n+3})=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Since
<math id="S4.SS1.p21.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{4}\sim r_{2},\pi_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{4}\sim r_{2},\pi_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="S4.SS1.p21.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(\ell_{4})=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(\ell_{4})=2</annotation></semantics></math>. The neighbors
<math id="S4.SS1.p21.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{n+3},\pi_{3},\ell_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{n+3},\pi_{3},\ell_{4}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S4.SS1.p21.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{n+2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{n+2}</annotation></semantics></math> use colors
<math id="S4.SS1.p21.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0,1,2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0,1,2</annotation></semantics></math>, a contradiction. This proves Claim 4.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p22" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p22.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p22.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Claim 3, one of <math id="S4.SS1.p22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2},\ell_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2},\ell_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> has color <math id="S4.SS1.p22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>; both vertices are
adjacent to <math id="S4.SS1.p22.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{6}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since
<math id="S4.SS1.p22.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{n+2}\sim\pi_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{n+2}\sim\pi_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have
<math id="S4.SS1.p22.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(\beta_{n+2})\in\{1,2\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(\beta_{n+2})\in\{1,2\}</annotation></semantics></math>. If
<math id="S4.SS1.p22.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(\beta_{n+2})=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(\beta_{n+2})=2</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S4.SS1.p22.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{6}</annotation></semantics></math> has a neighbor of
color <math id="S4.SS1.p22.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>, namely <math id="S4.SS1.p22.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{n+2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{n+2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Suppose instead that
<math id="S4.SS1.p22.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(\beta_{n+2})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(\beta_{n+2})=1</annotation></semantics></math>. Claim 2 and
<math id="S4.SS1.p22.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{n+2}\sim\gamma_{n+3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{n+2}\sim\gamma_{n+3}</annotation></semantics></math> imply
<math id="S4.SS1.p22.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(\gamma_{n+3})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(\gamma_{n+3})=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S4.SS1.p22.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{4}\sim\pi_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{4}\sim\pi_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have
<math id="S4.SS1.p22.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(\ell_{4})\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(\ell_{4})\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="S4.SS1.p22.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(\ell_{4})=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(\ell_{4})=2</annotation></semantics></math>, the neighbors
<math id="S4.SS1.p22.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{n+3},\pi_{3},\ell_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{n+3},\pi_{3},\ell_{4}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S4.SS1.p22.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{n+2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{n+2}</annotation></semantics></math> have colors
<math id="S4.SS1.p22.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0,1,2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0,1,2</annotation></semantics></math>, a contradiction. Hence <math id="S4.SS1.p22.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(\ell_{4})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(\ell_{4})=1</annotation></semantics></math>, and the
neighbors <math id="S4.SS1.p22.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{n+3},\ell_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{n+3},\ell_{4}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S4.SS1.p22.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> have colors <math id="S4.SS1.p22.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0,1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0,1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus <math id="S4.SS1.p22.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(r_{2})=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(r_{2})=2</annotation></semantics></math>. In this case, <math id="S4.SS1.p22.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is a neighbor of
<math id="S4.SS1.p22.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{6}</annotation></semantics></math> with color <math id="S4.SS1.p22.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p23" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p23.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p23.1.1" class="ltx_text">In both cases, <math id="S4.SS1.p23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{6}</annotation></semantics></math> has neighbors of colors <math id="S4.SS1.p23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS1.p23.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>, so
<math id="S4.SS1.p23.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(\ell_{6})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(\ell_{6})=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Each of
<math id="S4.SS1.p23.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2},\ell_{3},r_{2},\beta_{n+2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2},\ell_{3},r_{2},\beta_{n+2}</annotation></semantics></math> is adjacent to <math id="S4.SS1.p23.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{6}</annotation></semantics></math>, so none
has color <math id="S4.SS1.p23.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>. By Claim 4,
<math id="S4.SS1.p23.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(r_{2})=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(r_{2})=2</annotation></semantics></math>. By Claim 3, one of <math id="S4.SS1.p23.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2},\ell_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2},\ell_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> has color
<math id="S4.SS1.p23.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>. This vertex, <math id="S4.SS1.p23.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S4.SS1.p23.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> are three differently
colored neighbors of <math id="S4.SS1.p23.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{5}</annotation></semantics></math>, a contradiction.
Thus <math id="S4.SS1.p23.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{E_{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{E_{n}}</annotation></semantics></math> is not
<math id="S4.SS1.p23.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>-colorable.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
