<div id="S4.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 4.3</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For every <math id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{F_{n}}\subseteq\Gamma(\mathsf{V}\times F_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖵</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{F_{n}}\subseteq\Gamma(\mathsf{V}\times F_{n})</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{F_{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{F_{n}}</annotation></semantics></math> is not
<math id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>-colorable.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="S4.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Critical pairs.</em>
The minimal and maximal elements of <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> are</p>
<table id="S4.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Min(F_{n})=\{c,a_{n+2}\},\qquad\Max(F_{n})=\{b_{1},e\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Min(F_{n})=\{c,a_{n+2}\},\qquad\Max(F_{n})=\{b_{1},e\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">For <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq i\leq n+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq i\leq n+1</annotation></semantics></math>, condition (<a href="#S3.E5" title="In item (i) ‣ Lemma 3.1. ‣ 3 Critical pairs in 𝖵×𝑅 ‣ The Kelly–Trotter product conjecture for posets of dimension three" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>)
for <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> follows from</p>
<table id="S4.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}\nleq d,\qquad\mathord{\downarrow}^{\!\circ}a_{i}=\{c\}\subseteq\downarrow d,\qquad\mathord{\uparrow}^{\!\circ}d=\{e\}\subseteq\uparrow a_{i}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≰</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">↓</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">↑</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}\nleq d,\qquad\mathord{\downarrow}^{\!\circ}a_{i}=\{c\}\subseteq\downarrow d,\qquad\mathord{\uparrow}^{\!\circ}d=\{e\}\subseteq\uparrow a_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p">For <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{n+2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{n+2}</annotation></semantics></math>, the same condition follows from</p>
<table id="S4.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{n+2}\nleq d,\qquad\mathord{\downarrow}^{\!\circ}a_{n+2}=\varnothing,\qquad\mathord{\uparrow}^{\!\circ}d=\{e\}\subseteq\uparrow a_{n+2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≰</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">↓</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">↑</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{n+2}\nleq d,\qquad\mathord{\downarrow}^{\!\circ}a_{n+2}=\varnothing,\qquad\mathord{\uparrow}^{\!\circ}d=\{e\}\subseteq\uparrow a_{n+2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.4" class="ltx_p">For <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have
<math id="S4.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\nleq b_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≰</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\nleq b_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S4.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathord{\downarrow}^{\!\circ}d=\{c\}\subseteq\downarrow b_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">↓</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathord{\downarrow}^{\!\circ}d=\{c\}\subseteq\downarrow b_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.
If <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is maximal. If <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\leq i\leq n+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\leq i\leq n+2</annotation></semantics></math>, then
<math id="S4.SS2.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathord{\uparrow}^{\!\circ}b_{i}=\{e\}\subseteq\uparrow d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">↑</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathord{\uparrow}^{\!\circ}b_{i}=\{e\}\subseteq\uparrow d</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus condition (<a href="#S3.E5" title="In item (i) ‣ Lemma 3.1. ‣ 3 Critical pairs in 𝖵×𝑅 ‣ The Kelly–Trotter product conjecture for posets of dimension three" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>) also holds for every
<math id="S4.SS2.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, the first <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>-coordinate is
minimal, the second is maximal, and the two are incomparable.
Hence condition (<a href="#S3.E5" title="In item (i) ‣ Lemma 3.1. ‣ 3 Critical pairs in 𝖵×𝑅 ‣ The Kelly–Trotter product conjecture for posets of dimension three" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>) holds for these two
vertices.
For <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{1},r_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{1},r_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, condition (<a href="#S3.E5" title="In item (i) ‣ Lemma 3.1. ‣ 3 Critical pairs in 𝖵×𝑅 ‣ The Kelly–Trotter product conjecture for posets of dimension three" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>)
follows from</p>
<table id="S4.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{array}[]{llll}r_{1}:&amp;b_{1}\nleq e,&amp;\mathord{\downarrow}^{\!\circ}b_{1}=\{c,a_{1}\}\subseteq\downarrow e,&amp;\mathord{\uparrow}^{\!\circ}e=\varnothing,\\
r_{2}:&amp;c\nleq a_{n+2},&amp;\mathord{\downarrow}^{\!\circ}c=\varnothing,&amp;\mathord{\uparrow}^{\!\circ}a_{n+2}=\{b_{n+2},e\}\subseteq\uparrow c.\end{array}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≰</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">↓</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">↑</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>≰</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">↓</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">↑</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{array}[]{llll}r_{1}:&amp;b_{1}\nleq e,&amp;\mathord{\downarrow}^{\!\circ}b_{1}=\{c,a_{1}\}\subseteq\downarrow e,&amp;\mathord{\uparrow}^{\!\circ}e=\varnothing,\\
r_{2}:&amp;c\nleq a_{n+2},&amp;\mathord{\downarrow}^{\!\circ}c=\varnothing,&amp;\mathord{\uparrow}^{\!\circ}a_{n+2}=\{b_{n+2},e\}\subseteq\uparrow c.\end{array}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.5" class="ltx_p">By Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 3.1. ‣ 3 Critical pairs in 𝖵×𝑅 ‣ The Kelly–Trotter product conjecture for posets of dimension three" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>(i),
<math id="S4.SS2.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{i},\beta_{i},\ell_{1},\ell_{2},r_{1},r_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{i},\beta_{i},\ell_{1},\ell_{2},r_{1},r_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> are critical pairs.
Since <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\leq b_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\leq b_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\leq e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\leq e</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{n+2}\leq e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{n+2}\leq e</annotation></semantics></math>,
Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 3.1. ‣ 3 Critical pairs in 𝖵×𝑅 ‣ The Kelly–Trotter product conjecture for posets of dimension three" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>(ii) shows that
<math id="S4.SS2.p3.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{1},\pi_{2},\pi_{3},\pi_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{1},\pi_{2},\pi_{3},\pi_{4}</annotation></semantics></math> are critical pairs.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="S4.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Edges.</em>
By the Hasse diagram of <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, the two <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>-comparisons in
(<a href="#S3.E7" title="In 3 Critical pairs in 𝖵×𝑅 ‣ The Kelly–Trotter product conjecture for posets of dimension three" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>) hold for every adjacency in the right table.
Hence</p>
<table id="S4.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{F_{n}}\subseteq\Gamma(\mathsf{V}\times F_{n})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖵</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{F_{n}}\subseteq\Gamma(\mathsf{V}\times F_{n}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Suppose that <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math> is a proper <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>-coloring of <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{F_{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{F_{n}}</annotation></semantics></math>
with colors <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0,1,2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0,1,2</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Claim 1.</span>
All <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> have the same color. All <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> have the same
color. These two colors and <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(\pi_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(\pi_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> are distinct.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq i\leq n+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq i\leq n+1</annotation></semantics></math>. The vertices <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>
are adjacent. Both <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i+1}</annotation></semantics></math> are adjacent to
these two vertices. Hence
<math id="S4.SS2.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(\beta_{i})=\varphi(\beta_{i+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(\beta_{i})=\varphi(\beta_{i+1})</annotation></semantics></math>. Applying this equality for
all <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> gives</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(\beta_{1})=\cdots=\varphi(\beta_{n+2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(\beta_{1})=\cdots=\varphi(\beta_{n+2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">This color differs from <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(\pi_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(\pi_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>. For
<math id="S4.SS2.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq i\leq n+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq i\leq n+1</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{i}\sim\beta_{i},\pi_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{i}\sim\beta_{i},\pi_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{1},\ldots,\alpha_{n+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{1},\ldots,\alpha_{n+1}</annotation></semantics></math> have the third color. The
adjacencies <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{n+2}\sim\beta_{n+2},\pi_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{n+2}\sim\beta_{n+2},\pi_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> show that
<math id="S4.SS2.p7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{n+2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{n+2}</annotation></semantics></math> has the same third color. This proves Claim 1.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Claim 1, we may take</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(\beta_{i})=0\quad(1\leq i\leq n+2),\qquad\varphi(\alpha_{i})=1\quad(1\leq i\leq n+2),\qquad\varphi(\pi_{1})=2." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(\beta_{i})=0\quad(1\leq i\leq n+2),\qquad\varphi(\alpha_{i})=1\quad(1\leq i\leq n+2),\qquad\varphi(\pi_{1})=2.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{4}\sim\pi_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{4}\sim\pi_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have
<math id="S4.SS2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(\pi_{4})\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(\pi_{4})\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Claim 2.</span>
