<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 4.4</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For every <math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{G_{n}}\subseteq\Gamma(\mathsf{V}\times G_{n}),\qquad W_{J_{n}}\subseteq\Gamma(\mathsf{V}\times J_{n})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖵</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖵</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{G_{n}}\subseteq\Gamma(\mathsf{V}\times G_{n}),\qquad W_{J_{n}}\subseteq\Gamma(\mathsf{V}\times J_{n}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and neither <math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{G_{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{G_{n}}</annotation></semantics></math> nor <math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{J_{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{J_{n}}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>-colorable.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="S4.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Critical pairs.</em> Fix <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\in\{G_{n},J_{n}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\in\{G_{n},J_{n}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The minimal and maximal elements are</p>
<table id="S4.Ex38" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex38X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex38X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Min(G_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Min(G_{n})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex38X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\{a_{1},b_{1}\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\{a_{1},b_{1}\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex38X.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Max(G_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Max(G_{n})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex38X.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\{a_{n+3},b_{n+3}\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\{a_{n+3},b_{n+3}\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex38Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex38Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Min(J_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Min(J_{n})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex38Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\{a_{1},b_{1},c\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\{a_{1},b_{1},c\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex38Xa.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Max(J_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Max(J_{n})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex38Xa.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\{a_{n+3},b_{n+3},d\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\{a_{n+3},b_{n+3},d\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p4.2" class="ltx_p">In both <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S4.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a_{i}\leq_{R}b_{j}\iff j\geq i+1,\qquad b_{i}\leq_{R}a_{j}\iff j\geq i+2." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>R</mi></msub><mi>b</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>b</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>R</mi></msub><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}\leq_{R}b_{j}\iff j\geq i+1,\qquad b_{i}\leq_{R}a_{j}\iff j\geq i+2.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p4.3" class="ltx_p">By these relations, condition (<a href="#S3.E5" title="In item (i) ‣ Lemma 3.1. ‣ 3 Critical pairs in 𝖵×𝑅 ‣ The Kelly–Trotter product conjecture for posets of dimension three" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>) holds
for <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{array}[]{llll}\alpha_{i}:&amp;a_{i}\nleq_{R}b_{i},&amp;\mathord{\downarrow}^{\!\circ}a_{i}\subseteq\downarrow b_{i},&amp;\mathord{\uparrow}^{\!\circ}b_{i}\subseteq\uparrow a_{i},\\
\beta_{i}:&amp;b_{i}\nleq_{R}a_{i+1},&amp;\mathord{\downarrow}^{\!\circ}b_{i}\subseteq\downarrow a_{i+1},&amp;\mathord{\uparrow}^{\!\circ}a_{i+1}\subseteq\uparrow b_{i}.\end{array}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≰</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>R</mi></msub><mi>b</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">↓</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">↑</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>b</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≰</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>R</mi></msub><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">↓</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">↑</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{array}[]{llll}\alpha_{i}:&amp;a_{i}\nleq_{R}b_{i},&amp;\mathord{\downarrow}^{\!\circ}a_{i}\subseteq\downarrow b_{i},&amp;\mathord{\uparrow}^{\!\circ}b_{i}\subseteq\uparrow a_{i},\\
\beta_{i}:&amp;b_{i}\nleq_{R}a_{i+1},&amp;\mathord{\downarrow}^{\!\circ}b_{i}\subseteq\downarrow a_{i+1},&amp;\mathord{\uparrow}^{\!\circ}a_{i+1}\subseteq\uparrow b_{i}.\end{array}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p4.4" class="ltx_p">For <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, condition (<a href="#S3.E5" title="In item (i) ‣ Lemma 3.1. ‣ 3 Critical pairs in 𝖵×𝑅 ‣ The Kelly–Trotter product conjecture for posets of dimension three" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>) for
<math id="S4.SS3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{1},r_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{1},r_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> follows from</p>
<table id="S4.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{array}[]{llll}r_{1}:&amp;c\nleq a_{n+3},&amp;\mathord{\downarrow}^{\!\circ}c=\{a_{1}\}\subseteq\downarrow a_{n+3},&amp;\mathord{\uparrow}^{\!\circ}a_{n+3}=\varnothing,\\
r_{2}:&amp;b_{1}\nleq c,&amp;\mathord{\downarrow}^{\!\circ}b_{1}=\varnothing,&amp;\mathord{\uparrow}^{\!\circ}c=\{b_{n+3}\}\subseteq\uparrow b_{1}.\end{array}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>≰</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">↓</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">↑</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≰</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">↓</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">↑</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{array}[]{llll}r_{1}:&amp;c\nleq a_{n+3},&amp;\mathord{\downarrow}^{\!\circ}c=\{a_{1}\}\subseteq\downarrow a_{n+3},&amp;\mathord{\uparrow}^{\!\circ}a_{n+3}=\varnothing,\\
r_{2}:&amp;b_{1}\nleq c,&amp;\mathord{\downarrow}^{\!\circ}b_{1}=\varnothing,&amp;\mathord{\uparrow}^{\!\circ}c=\{b_{n+3}\}\subseteq\uparrow b_{1}.\end{array}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p4.5" class="ltx_p">For <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, the two coordinate pairs used by <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{1},r_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{1},r_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> are
<math id="S4.SS3.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\parallel a_{n+3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\parallel a_{n+3}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{1}\parallel d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{1}\parallel d</annotation></semantics></math>. Each is an
incomparable pair in <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Min(J_{n})\times\Max(J_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mi>Max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Min(J_{n})\times\Max(J_{n})</annotation></semantics></math>, so
condition (<a href="#S3.E5" title="In item (i) ‣ Lemma 3.1. ‣ 3 Critical pairs in 𝖵×𝑅 ‣ The Kelly–Trotter product conjecture for posets of dimension three" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>) holds.
By Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 3.1. ‣ 3 Critical pairs in 𝖵×𝑅 ‣ The Kelly–Trotter product conjecture for posets of dimension three" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>(i),
<math id="S4.SS3.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{i},\beta_{i},r_{1},r_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{i},\beta_{i},r_{1},r_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> are critical pairs. Since
<math id="S4.SS3.p4.m14" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a_{1}\leq_{R}a_{n+3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>R</mi></msub><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1}\leq_{R}a_{n+3}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m15" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="b_{1}\leq_{R}b_{n+3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>R</mi></msub><mi>b</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{1}\leq_{R}b_{n+3}</annotation></semantics></math>, and
<math id="S4.SS3.p4.m16" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a_{1}\leq_{R}b_{n+3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>R</mi></msub><mi>b</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1}\leq_{R}b_{n+3}</annotation></semantics></math>,
Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 3.1. ‣ 3 Critical pairs in 𝖵×𝑅 ‣ The Kelly–Trotter product conjecture for posets of dimension three" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>(ii) shows that
<math id="S4.SS3.p4.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{1},\pi_{2},\pi_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{1},\pi_{2},\pi_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> are critical pairs.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="S4.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Edges.</em>
By the two Hasse diagrams, all comparisons in
(<a href="#S3.E7" title="In 3 Critical pairs in 𝖵×𝑅 ‣ The Kelly–Trotter product conjecture for posets of dimension three" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>) hold for the adjacencies in the right table.
Hence</p>
<table id="S4.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{G_{n}}\subseteq\Gamma(\mathsf{V}\times G_{n}),\qquad W_{J_{n}}\subseteq\Gamma(\mathsf{V}\times J_{n})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖵</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖵</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{G_{n}}\subseteq\Gamma(\mathsf{V}\times G_{n}),\qquad W_{J_{n}}\subseteq\Gamma(\mathsf{V}\times J_{n}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S4.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> be either <math id="S4.SS3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{G_{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{G_{n}}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S4.SS3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{J_{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{J_{n}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and suppose that
<math id="S4.SS3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math> is a proper <math id="S4.SS3.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>-coloring of <math id="S4.SS3.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> with colors <math id="S4.SS3.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0,1,2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0,1,2</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Claim.</span>
<math id="S4.SS3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(\pi_{1})\neq\varphi(\pi_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(\pi_{1})\neq\varphi(\pi_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Assume that
<math id="S4.SS3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(\pi_{1})=\varphi(\pi_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(\pi_{1})=\varphi(\pi_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>. Every vertex of the odd cycle is
adjacent to at least one of <math id="S4.SS3.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{1},\pi_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{1},\pi_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, so no vertex of the cycle
can receive their common color. Hence the cycle uses only the other two
colors. This would be a proper <math id="S4.SS3.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>-coloring of an odd cycle, which is
impossible.
This proves the claim.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">By the claim, we may take</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(\pi_{1})=0,\qquad\varphi(\pi_{2})=1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(\pi_{1})=0,\qquad\varphi(\pi_{2})=1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">Then</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex44" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex44X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex44X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\alpha_{2}\sim\pi_{1},\pi_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\alpha_{2}\sim\pi_{1},\pi_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex44X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Longrightarrow\varphi(\alpha_{2})=2," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Longrightarrow\varphi(\alpha_{2})=2,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex44Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex44Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\beta_{1}\sim\pi_{1},\alpha_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\beta_{1}\sim\pi_{1},\alpha_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex44Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Longrightarrow\varphi(\beta_{1})=1." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Longrightarrow\varphi(\beta_{1})=1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p9.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p9.3.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="S4.SS3.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, the neighbors <math id="S4.SS3.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{1},\pi_{2},\alpha_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{1},\pi_{2},\alpha_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> of
<math id="S4.SS3.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> have colors <math id="S4.SS3.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0,1,2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0,1,2</annotation></semantics></math>, a contradiction.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S4.SS3.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=0</annotation></semantics></math>. We have</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{2}\sim\pi_{2},\alpha_{2}\quad\Longrightarrow\quad\varphi(\beta_{2})=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{2}\sim\pi_{2},\alpha_{2}\quad\Longrightarrow\quad\varphi(\beta_{2})=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">The neighbors <math id="S4.SS3.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{2},\beta_{1},\alpha_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{2},\beta_{1},\alpha_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S4.SS3.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> have colors
<math id="S4.SS3.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0,1,2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0,1,2</annotation></semantics></math>, again a contradiction.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.4 </span>The family <math id="S4.SS4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{n}</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

