<div id="S4.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 4.5</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For every <math id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{H_{n}}\subseteq\Gamma(\mathsf{V}\times H_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖵</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{H_{n}}\subseteq\Gamma(\mathsf{V}\times H_{n})</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{H_{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{H_{n}}</annotation></semantics></math> is not
<math id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>-colorable.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="S4.SS4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Critical pairs.</em>
The minimal and maximal elements of <math id="S4.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> are</p>
<table id="S4.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Min(H_{n})=\{a_{1},b_{1},d\},\qquad\Max(H_{n})=\{a_{n+2},b_{n+3},c\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Min(H_{n})=\{a_{1},b_{1},d\},\qquad\Max(H_{n})=\{a_{n+2},b_{n+3},c\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.p3.2" class="ltx_p">In <math id="S4.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S4.Ex47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}\leq b_{j}\iff j\geq i+2,\qquad b_{i}\leq a_{j}\iff j\geq i+1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}\leq b_{j}\iff j\geq i+2,\qquad b_{i}\leq a_{j}\iff j\geq i+1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.p3.3" class="ltx_p">By these formulas, condition (<a href="#S3.E5" title="In item (i) ‣ Lemma 3.1. ‣ 3 Critical pairs in 𝖵×𝑅 ‣ The Kelly–Trotter product conjecture for posets of dimension three" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>) holds
for <math id="S4.SS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{array}[]{llll}\alpha_{i}:&amp;a_{i}\nleq b_{i+1},&amp;\mathord{\downarrow}^{\!\circ}a_{i}\subseteq\downarrow b_{i+1},&amp;\mathord{\uparrow}^{\!\circ}b_{i+1}\subseteq\uparrow a_{i},\\
\beta_{i}:&amp;b_{i}\nleq a_{i},&amp;\mathord{\downarrow}^{\!\circ}b_{i}\subseteq\downarrow a_{i},&amp;\mathord{\uparrow}^{\!\circ}a_{i}\subseteq\uparrow b_{i}.\end{array}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≰</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">↓</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">↑</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≰</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">↓</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">↑</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{array}[]{llll}\alpha_{i}:&amp;a_{i}\nleq b_{i+1},&amp;\mathord{\downarrow}^{\!\circ}a_{i}\subseteq\downarrow b_{i+1},&amp;\mathord{\uparrow}^{\!\circ}b_{i+1}\subseteq\uparrow a_{i},\\
\beta_{i}:&amp;b_{i}\nleq a_{i},&amp;\mathord{\downarrow}^{\!\circ}b_{i}\subseteq\downarrow a_{i},&amp;\mathord{\uparrow}^{\!\circ}a_{i}\subseteq\uparrow b_{i}.\end{array}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.p3.4" class="ltx_p">For each of <math id="S4.SS4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{1},\ldots,\ell_{6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>6</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{1},\ldots,\ell_{6}</annotation></semantics></math>, the first <math id="S4.SS4.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>-coordinate is
minimal, the second is maximal, and the two are incomparable. Thus
condition (<a href="#S3.E5" title="In item (i) ‣ Lemma 3.1. ‣ 3 Critical pairs in 𝖵×𝑅 ‣ The Kelly–Trotter product conjecture for posets of dimension three" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>) holds for these six
vertices. For <math id="S4.SS4.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{1},r_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{1},r_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, the same condition follows from</p>
<table id="S4.Ex49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{array}[]{llll}r_{1}:&amp;b_{1}\nleq d,&amp;\mathord{\downarrow}^{\!\circ}b_{1}=\varnothing,&amp;\mathord{\uparrow}^{\!\circ}d=\{b_{n+3}\}\subseteq\uparrow b_{1},\\
r_{2}:&amp;c\nleq b_{n+3},&amp;\mathord{\downarrow}^{\!\circ}c=\{b_{1}\}\subseteq\downarrow b_{n+3},&amp;\mathord{\uparrow}^{\!\circ}b_{n+3}=\varnothing.\end{array}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≰</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">↓</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">↑</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>≰</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">↓</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">↑</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{array}[]{llll}r_{1}:&amp;b_{1}\nleq d,&amp;\mathord{\downarrow}^{\!\circ}b_{1}=\varnothing,&amp;\mathord{\uparrow}^{\!\circ}d=\{b_{n+3}\}\subseteq\uparrow b_{1},\\
r_{2}:&amp;c\nleq b_{n+3},&amp;\mathord{\downarrow}^{\!\circ}c=\{b_{1}\}\subseteq\downarrow b_{n+3},&amp;\mathord{\uparrow}^{\!\circ}b_{n+3}=\varnothing.\end{array}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.p3.5" class="ltx_p">By Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 3.1. ‣ 3 Critical pairs in 𝖵×𝑅 ‣ The Kelly–Trotter product conjecture for posets of dimension three" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>(i),
<math id="S4.SS4.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{i},\beta_{i},\ell_{1},\ldots,\ell_{6},r_{1},r_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{i},\beta_{i},\ell_{1},\ldots,\ell_{6},r_{1},r_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> are critical pairs.
Since <math id="S4.SS4.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{1}\leq b_{n+3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1}\leq b_{n+3}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS4.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{1}\leq a_{n+2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{1}\leq a_{n+2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and
<math id="S4.SS4.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{1}\leq b_{n+3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{1}\leq b_{n+3}</annotation></semantics></math>,
Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 3.1. ‣ 3 Critical pairs in 𝖵×𝑅 ‣ The Kelly–Trotter product conjecture for posets of dimension three" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>(ii) shows that
<math id="S4.SS4.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{1},\pi_{2},\pi_{3},\pi_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{1},\pi_{2},\pi_{3},\pi_{4}</annotation></semantics></math> are critical pairs.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="S4.SS4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Edges.</em>
By the Hasse diagram of <math id="S4.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, the two comparisons in
(<a href="#S3.E7" title="In 3 Critical pairs in 𝖵×𝑅 ‣ The Kelly–Trotter product conjecture for posets of dimension three" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>) hold for every adjacency in the right table.
Hence</p>
<table id="S4.Ex50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{H_{n}}\subseteq\Gamma(\mathsf{V}\times H_{n})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖵</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{H_{n}}\subseteq\Gamma(\mathsf{V}\times H_{n}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Suppose that <math id="S4.SS4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math> is a proper <math id="S4.SS4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>-coloring of <math id="S4.SS4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{H_{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{H_{n}}</annotation></semantics></math> with
colors <math id="S4.SS4.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0,1,2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0,1,2</annotation></semantics></math>. We may take <math id="S4.SS4.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(\pi_{1})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(\pi_{1})=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Since
<math id="S4.SS4.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{1}\sim\pi_{2},\pi_{3},\pi_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{1}\sim\pi_{2},\pi_{3},\pi_{4}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(\pi_{2}),\varphi(\pi_{3}),\varphi(\pi_{4})\in\{1,2\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(\pi_{2}),\varphi(\pi_{3}),\varphi(\pi_{4})\in\{1,2\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS4.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Claim.</span>
The vertices <math id="S4.SS4.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{2},\pi_{3},\pi_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{2},\pi_{3},\pi_{4}</annotation></semantics></math> have the same color.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Assume that <math id="S4.SS4.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{2},\pi_{3},\pi_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{2},\pi_{3},\pi_{4}</annotation></semantics></math> do not all have the same color. We may take
<math id="S4.SS4.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(\pi_{2})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(\pi_{2})=1</annotation></semantics></math>. We consider the three possible pairs
<math id="S4.SS4.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\varphi(\pi_{3}),\varphi(\pi_{4}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\varphi(\pi_{3}),\varphi(\pi_{4}))</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS4.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="S4.SS4.p8.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Case 1: <math id="S4.SS4.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1,2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1,2)</annotation></semantics></math>.</em></p>
<table id="S4.Ex52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{n+2}\sim\pi_{2},\pi_{4}\quad\Longrightarrow\quad\varphi(\beta_{n+2})=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{n+2}\sim\pi_{2},\pi_{4}\quad\Longrightarrow\quad\varphi(\beta_{n+2})=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.p8.2" class="ltx_p">If <math id="S4.SS4.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, the neighbors
<math id="S4.SS4.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{n+2},\pi_{2},\pi_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{n+2},\pi_{2},\pi_{4}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S4.SS4.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{n+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{n+1}</annotation></semantics></math> have colors
<math id="S4.SS4.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0,1,2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0,1,2</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="S4.SS4.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=0</annotation></semantics></math>, the neighbors
<math id="S4.SS4.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{2},\pi_{3},\pi_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{2},\pi_{3},\pi_{4}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S4.SS4.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> have colors <math id="S4.SS4.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0,1,2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0,1,2</annotation></semantics></math>.
Both alternatives are impossible.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS4.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="S4.SS4.p9.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Case 2: <math id="S4.SS4.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(2,2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(2,2)</annotation></semantics></math>.</em></p>
<table id="S4.Ex53" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex53X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex53X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\beta_{n+2}\sim\pi_{2},\pi_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\beta_{n+2}\sim\pi_{2},\pi_{4}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex53X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Longrightarrow\varphi(\beta_{n+2})=0," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Longrightarrow\varphi(\beta_{n+2})=0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex53Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex53Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ell_{2}\sim\pi_{2},\pi_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ell_{2}\sim\pi_{2},\pi_{4}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex53Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Longrightarrow\varphi(\ell_{2})=0," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Longrightarrow\varphi(\ell_{2})=0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex53Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex53Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\alpha_{n+2}\sim\beta_{n+2},\pi_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\alpha_{n+2}\sim\beta_{n+2},\pi_{3}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex53Xb.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Longrightarrow\varphi(\alpha_{n+2})=1," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Longrightarrow\varphi(\alpha_{n+2})=1,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex53Xc"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex53Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ell_{1}\sim\alpha_{n+2},\pi_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ell_{1}\sim\alpha_{n+2},\pi_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex53Xc.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Longrightarrow\varphi(\ell_{1})=2," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Longrightarrow\varphi(\ell_{1})=2,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex53Xd"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex53Xd.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r_{1}\sim\ell_{1},\ell_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r_{1}\sim\ell_{1},\ell_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex53Xd.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Longrightarrow\varphi(r_{1})=1," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Longrightarrow\varphi(r_{1})=1,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
