<p id="S4.SS5.p3.5" class="ltx_p">By Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 3.1. ‣ 3 Critical pairs in 𝖵×𝑅 ‣ The Kelly–Trotter product conjecture for posets of dimension three" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>(i),
<math id="S4.SS5.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{i},\beta_{i},r_{1},r_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{i},\beta_{i},r_{1},r_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> are critical pairs.
Since <math id="S4.SS5.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}\leq d_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}\leq d_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S4.SS5.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq i\leq n+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq i\leq n+1</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="S4.SS5.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{n+2}\leq d_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{n+2}\leq d_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS5.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\leq d_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\leq d_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S4.SS5.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\leq d_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\leq d_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>,
Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 3.1. ‣ 3 Critical pairs in 𝖵×𝑅 ‣ The Kelly–Trotter product conjecture for posets of dimension three" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>(ii) shows that
<math id="S4.SS5.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{1},\ldots,\gamma_{n+2},\pi_{1},\pi_{2},\pi_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{1},\ldots,\gamma_{n+2},\pi_{1},\pi_{2},\pi_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> are critical pairs.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS5.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="S4.SS5.p4.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Edges.</em>
By the Hasse diagram of <math id="S4.SS5.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, the two <math id="S4.SS5.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>-comparisons in
(<a href="#S3.E7" title="In 3 Critical pairs in 𝖵×𝑅 ‣ The Kelly–Trotter product conjecture for posets of dimension three" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>) hold for every adjacency in the right table.
Hence</p>
<table id="S4.Ex67" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{I_{n}}\subseteq\Gamma(\mathsf{V}\times I_{n})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖵</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{I_{n}}\subseteq\Gamma(\mathsf{V}\times I_{n}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS5.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Suppose that <math id="S4.SS5.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math> is a proper <math id="S4.SS5.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>-coloring of <math id="S4.SS5.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{I_{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{I_{n}}</annotation></semantics></math>
with colors <math id="S4.SS5.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0,1,2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0,1,2</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S4.SS5.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{1}\sim\pi_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{1}\sim\pi_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>, we may assume</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex68" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(\pi_{3})=0,\qquad\varphi(\pi_{1})=1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(\pi_{3})=0,\qquad\varphi(\pi_{1})=1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS5.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS5.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Each of <math id="S4.SS5.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{1},\ldots,\gamma_{n+2},\pi_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{1},\ldots,\gamma_{n+2},\pi_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is adjacent to
<math id="S4.SS5.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>, so these vertices have color <math id="S4.SS5.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S4.SS5.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS5.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS5.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Claim.</span>
<math id="S4.SS5.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(\pi_{2})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(\pi_{2})=1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS5.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Assume that <math id="S4.SS5.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(\pi_{2})=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(\pi_{2})=2</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="S4.SS5.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq i\leq n+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq i\leq n+2</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex69" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{i}\sim\pi_{1},\pi_{2}\quad\Longrightarrow\quad\varphi(\alpha_{i})=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{i}\sim\pi_{1},\pi_{2}\quad\Longrightarrow\quad\varphi(\alpha_{i})=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS5.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS5.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">The adjacencies <math id="S4.SS5.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1}\sim\alpha_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1}\sim\alpha_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S4.SS5.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i}\sim\alpha_{i-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i}\sim\alpha_{i-1}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S4.SS5.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\leq i\leq n+3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\leq i\leq n+3</annotation></semantics></math> exclude color
<math id="S4.SS5.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> from every <math id="S4.SS5.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS5.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">The edges</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex70" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i}\sim\gamma_{i}\quad\text{and}\quad\gamma_{i}\sim\beta_{i+1}\qquad(1\leq i\leq n+2)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i}\sim\gamma_{i}\quad\text{and}\quad\gamma_{i}\sim\beta_{i+1}\qquad(1\leq i\leq n+2)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS5.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS5.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">form a path from <math id="S4.SS5.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.SS5.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{n+3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{n+3}</annotation></semantics></math>. Every vertex on the
path has color <math id="S4.SS5.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S4.SS5.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>, so the colors alternate. The subpaths from
<math id="S4.SS5.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.SS5.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{n+3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{n+3}</annotation></semantics></math> and from <math id="S4.SS5.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> to
<math id="S4.SS5.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{n+2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{n+2}</annotation></semantics></math> each have <math id="S4.SS5.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2n+3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2n+3</annotation></semantics></math> edges. Thus</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex71" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\varphi(\beta_{n+3}),\varphi(\gamma_{1})\}=\{1,2\},\qquad\{\varphi(\beta_{1}),\varphi(\gamma_{n+2})\}=\{1,2\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\varphi(\beta_{n+3}),\varphi(\gamma_{1})\}=\{1,2\},\qquad\{\varphi(\beta_{1}),\varphi(\gamma_{n+2})\}=\{1,2\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS5.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS5.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">The two neighbors <math id="S4.SS5.p8.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{n+3},\gamma_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{n+3},\gamma_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S4.SS5.p8.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> use colors
<math id="S4.SS5.p8.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1,2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1,2</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="S4.SS5.p8.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(r_{2})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(r_{2})=0</annotation></semantics></math>. The neighbors
<math id="S4.SS5.p8.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{2},\beta_{1},\gamma_{n+2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{2},\beta_{1},\gamma_{n+2}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S4.SS5.p8.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> use all three colors, a
contradiction. This proves the claim.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS5.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S4.SS5.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{2}\sim\pi_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{2}\sim\pi_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have
<math id="S4.SS5.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(r_{2})\in\{0,2\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(r_{2})\in\{0,2\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS5.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Suppose first that <math id="S4.SS5.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(r_{2})=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(r_{2})=2</annotation></semantics></math>. We have</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex72" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex72X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
