</div>
<div id="S6.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">By the classification, choose a poset <math id="S6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> from the six infinite families
or the ten fixed posets such that <math id="S6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\cong S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>≅</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\cong S</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{d}\cong S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>≅</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{d}\cong S</annotation></semantics></math>.
Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 4.1. ‣ 4 The six infinite families ‣ The Kelly–Trotter product conjecture for posets of dimension three" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a> covers the infinite families, and
Proposition <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition 5.1. ‣ 5 Computer verification for the ten fixed posets ‣ The Kelly–Trotter product conjecture for posets of dimension three" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a> covers the fixed posets. Thus
<math id="S6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma(\mathsf{V}\times S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖵</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma(\mathsf{V}\times S)</annotation></semantics></math> is not <math id="S6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>-colorable.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="S6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\cong S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>≅</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\cong S</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S6.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma(\mathsf{V}\times R)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖵</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma(\mathsf{V}\times R)</annotation></semantics></math> is not
<math id="S6.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>-colorable. If <math id="S6.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{d}\cong S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>≅</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{d}\cong S</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
