<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex87.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dim(C_{k}\times R)=4." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">dim</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dim(C_{k}\times R)=4.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S6.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">The result follows from Theorem <a href="#S6.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 6.1. ‣ 6 Proofs of the main results ‣ The Kelly–Trotter product conjecture for posets of dimension three" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.1</span></a> and
Proposition <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition 3.2. ‣ 3 Critical pairs in 𝖵×𝑅 ‣ The Kelly–Trotter product conjecture for posets of dimension three" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 6.3</span></span><span id="S6.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S6.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> be finite posets. If <math id="S6.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dim P=\dim Q=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">dim</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.167em">dim</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dim P=\dim Q=3</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex88" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex88.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dim(P\times Q)\geq 4." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">dim</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dim(P\times Q)\geq 4.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S6.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Choose <math id="S6.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>-irreducible subposets <math id="S6.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{0}\subseteq P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{0}\subseteq P</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S6.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{0}\subseteq Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{0}\subseteq Q</annotation></semantics></math>. By monotonicity, it suffices to prove
<math id="S6.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dim(P_{0}\times Q_{0})\geq 4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">dim</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dim(P_{0}\times Q_{0})\geq 4</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S6.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">If both <math id="S6.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> are crowns, the result follows from
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>, Proposition 19]</cite>. If exactly one is a crown,
Corollary <a href="#S6.Thmtheorem2" title="Corollary 6.2. ‣ 6 Proofs of the main results ‣ The Kelly–Trotter product conjecture for posets of dimension three" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.2</span></a> applies. Suppose neither is a crown.
Each contains a subposet isomorphic to one of <math id="S6.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{3},Z_{3}^{d},C_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mn>3</mn><mi>d</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{3},Z_{3}^{d},C_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Choose such subposets <math id="S6.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\subseteq P_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\subseteq P_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y\subseteq Q_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y\subseteq Q_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Up to factor exchange and duality, <math id="S6.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\times Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\times Y</annotation></semantics></math> is one of</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex89" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex89.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{3}\times Z_{3},\qquad Z_{3}\times Z_{3}^{d},\qquad Z_{3}\times C_{2},\qquad C_{2}\times C_{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mn>3</mn><mi>d</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{3}\times Z_{3},\qquad Z_{3}\times Z_{3}^{d},\qquad Z_{3}\times C_{2},\qquad C_{2}\times C_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Each product has dimension at least four <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite>.
Hence</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex90" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex90.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4\leq\dim(X\times Y)\leq\dim(P_{0}\times Q_{0})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">dim</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">dim</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4\leq\dim(X\times Y)\leq\dim(P_{0}\times Q_{0}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">as required.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 6.4</span></span><span id="S6.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S6.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> be a finite poset of dimension three. For every <math id="S6.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex91" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex91.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dim(C_{k}\times P)=4." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">dim</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dim(C_{k}\times P)=4.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S6.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Theorem <a href="#S6.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 6.3. ‣ 6 Proofs of the main results ‣ The Kelly–Trotter product conjecture for posets of dimension three" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.3</span></a> and (<a href="#S1.E2" title="In 1 Introduction ‣ The Kelly–Trotter product conjecture for posets of dimension three" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) give</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex92" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex92.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4\leq\dim(C_{k}\times P)=\dim(P\times C_{k})\leq\max\{3,\dim P+1\}=4." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">dim</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">dim</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">dim</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4\leq\dim(C_{k}\times P)=\dim(P\times C_{k})\leq\max\{3,\dim P+1\}=4.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
